    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pairs\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThis plugin works like a charm but has one feature that is missing (and one that overlaps with mini.surround).\r\n\r\nLet's imagine this Python code:\r\n```py\r\nprint(hello_world)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I position my cursor between `(` and `h` and then add a quote mark or parenthesis, we will get this:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nprint(''hello_world)\r\n```\r\nor\r\n```py\r\nprint(()hello_world)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be great if there was a way to configure the plugin so that it wraps words that start with alphanumerics instead of adding pairs.\r\n\r\nSo in same scenario:\r\n\r\n> If I position my cursor between `(` and `h` and then add a quote mark or parenthesis, we will get this:\r\n\r\nOutcome will be:\r\n```py\r\nprint('hello_world')\r\n```\r\nor\r\n```py\r\nprint((hello_world))\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote1: Perhaps such configuration in the current plugin version is achievable already?\r\nNote2: I know I can achieve the same with mini.surround.\r\nNote3: Also I am aware there is this ticket -> https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/835\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, this use case is a bit different than what 835 wants to achieve.",
