        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> Note1: Perhaps such configuration in the current plugin version is achievable already?\r\n\r\nI am afraid there is none and never will be. This is because 'mini.pairs' intentionally works **only** with inside a two character neighborhood (one to the left and one to the right) and **only** with a two character pair (one open and one close).\r\n\r\n> Note2: I know I can achieve the same with mini.surround.\r\n\r\nIndeed, and my suggestion is to use 'mini.surround' for that.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
